1. Security and Privacy Protection Requirements
 User Authentication:
The system must implement multi-factor authentication with at least two factors for customer accounts, with a successful authentication rate of at least 99.9% for legitimate users and must prevent 99.99% of unauthorized access attempts.
Data Encryption:
All sensitive customer data (personal information, payment details, booking history) must be encrypted in transit and at rest using industry-standard encryption (minimum AES-256 for data at rest and TLS 1.3 for data in transit), with encryption implementation verified through security penetration testing.
Privacy Controls:
Customers must be able to access, modify, and delete their personal data, with all personal data deletion requests processed within 72 hours and confirmed with an audit trail.
Authorization Controls:
The system must enforce proper access controls ensuring customers can only access and modify their own data, with zero instances of unauthorized cross-account access in monthly security audits.
Data Breach Detection:
The system must detect and alert on potential data breaches within 5 minutes of suspicious activity with a false positive rate below 0.1%.

2. Performance Requirements
Response Time:
The restaurant search functionality must return results within 2 seconds for at least 95% of search queries under normal load conditions (up to 1000 concurrent users).
UI Responsiveness:
All user interface interactions within the mobile app must respond within 500 milliseconds for 98% of interactions on devices released within the past three years.
Booking Confirmation:
Table booking confirmations must be processed and displayed to the customer within 3 seconds of submission for at least 99% of booking attempts.
Location Services:
Location-based restaurant searches must identify and display restaurants within a specified radius in under 4 seconds for 95% of searches, with location accuracy within 50 meters.
Image Loading:
Food and restaurant images must load within 4 seconds on standard mobile network connections (minimum 3G) for 90% of image requests.

3. Reliability Requirements
System Uptime:
The CloudTables-Customer mobile app must maintain 99.9% uptime, measured monthly, excluding scheduled maintenance periods (limited to no more than 2 hours per month during off-peak hours).
Booking Accuracy:
The system must maintain 100% accuracy of table booking information across all integrated systems, with automated verification checks running every 5 minutes.
Fault Tolerance:
The mobile app must gracefully handle connectivity issues by queuing customer actions locally and synchronizing once connectivity is restored, with 99% of temporarily offline actions successfully completed when connectivity returns.
Data Consistency:
The system must maintain data consistency between the mobile app cache and backend systems with a maximum divergence time of 30 seconds for 95% of data under normal operating conditions.
Error Recovery:
When system errors occur, the mobile app must automatically recover and return to a stable state without user intervention in 95% of error cases, with clear error messages provided in the remaining cases.

4. Scalability Requirements
Concurrent Users:
The CloudTables-Customer system must support at least 100,000 concurrent active users with no degradation in system response times specified in the performance requirements.
Transaction Volume:
The system must handle at least 5,000 bookings per minute during peak hours with no more than 0.1% failed booking attempts due to system limitations.
Search Query Processing:
The restaurant search functionality must support at least 10,000 complex search queries per minute with response times remaining within the parameters defined in QR-P-1.
Data Storage Growth:
The system must accommodate a 50% year-over-year growth in customer accounts and historical data without requiring architectural changes, only resource scaling.
Dynamic Resource Allocation:
The system must automatically scale computing resources up or down based on demand, with resource allocation changes completed within 2 minutes of detecting a sustained 20% change in system load.
